{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 400,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Have you ever wondered how the earth stays\nin orbit around the sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2760,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, the pull of gravity is stronger the\ncloser you are to the sun, so you'd think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6350,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that if the earth got bumped slightly towards\nthe sun (like, if you jumped, or something),"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9490,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the sun would pull just a little bit\nstronger, tugging the earth yet closer still,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12880,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at which point the sun's pull would be stronger\nyet again, … and the earth would spiral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16080,
    "dDurationMs": 1609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in to its eventual doom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17689,
    "dDurationMs": 3031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you and I and swiss cheese are clearly\nevidence that the earth doesn't just spiral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20720,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in to its doom – so why not?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22460,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, when the earth does get pushed a little\nbit towards the sun, the sun's pull speeds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26140,
    "dDurationMs": 3899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it up a little bit, too - so even though the\nnearby sun's pull is stronger, the earth will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30039,
    "dDurationMs": 3301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be going fast enough that it overshoots and\nends up farther away from the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33340,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, the sun's pull slows it down again\nin the process… at which point the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36770,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turns back and starts the cycle all over again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39040,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The amazing thing is that the two effects\nof speeding up plus stronger gravitational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42210,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attraction perfectly balance, so that the\nearth stays in its orbit the same way a marble"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46130,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stays at the bottom of a bowl even if it gets\nknocked around a little bit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49120,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This balance is very special indeed - it's\nhighly dependent on the strength of the gravitational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53010,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "force and the number of dimensions we live\nin, and in fact, these stable orbits only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56890,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exist in a three dimensional universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59040,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The details are a bit subtle, but if gravity\nwere just slightly steeper, as it would be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62250,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we lived in four spatial dimensions, you\ncould never orbit the sun because you'd get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65970,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pulled in without picking up enough speed\nto escape and you WOULD spiral in to your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69160,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70160,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if we lived in fewer dimensions so that\ngravity were a bit tamer, then you could ALSO"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73130,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never orbit the sun, because as you approached\nit, you wouldn't be pulled enough and would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76230,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "merely pass by with your path slightly bent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78510,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we're incredibly lucky to live in a three\ndimensional universe where there ARE stable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81670,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbits that allow planets, solar systems,\nand galaxies to exist at all!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84570,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you, stable orbits, for without you,\nlife as we know it, and especially cheese,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89380,
    "dDurationMs": 1779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91159,
    "dDurationMs": 3261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ps An awesome down-to-earth example of stable\norbits are the hyperbolic funnels that you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94420,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "often see at museums or in shopping malls:\nthe physics is almost identical to the stable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98390,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbits of planets, satellites, and moons,\nand the only reason the coins in the funnels"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101740,
    "dDurationMs": 3309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(or satellites around the earth) eventually\nDO spiral in to their doom is because they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105049,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lose energy to friction and thus shift down\nfrom one stable orbit to another, until eventually,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109479,
    "dDurationMs": 1881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their orbit coincides with the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111360,
    "dDurationMs": 850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is called crashing."
    } ]
  } ]
}
